Caption. Decided target of option B in the PROD environment only (owner, 2026-10-22), the target figure of the ARD (owner round r1, 2026-10-19; S2 2026-10-20).
D1 = B: one runtime, the Cloud Run backend (GenAiR FastAPI server) running the ADK agent in process, in the pro project of the PROD landing zone.
S3 = Pub/Sub: Chat app → events topic → push subscription (OIDC, dedicated push service account) → Google Chat API integration (`/gchat-push`,
event check and dedup, reply, 1–5 rating) → agent. S1 = RAG Engine. S2 = Firestore (`FirestoreSessionService`, `hrpn-sessions`, TTL for the 1-year history of HR04).
Layout after the Google Cloud standard landing zone: app project, Observability next to the CI/CD project, PROD SSM in the CI/CD project (ssm = cicd project).
Colours: blue = GenAiR standard; green = customisation within the GenAiR template frame, data services included; yellow = added outside the frame
(Pub/Sub, Google Chat API integration); no fill = Google or third-party managed service. HR01 = A without ChatUI: no load balancer, IAP or ADK web UI.
Open: gate G1 (publisher exception, VPC-SC), PROD project ids, SCM host, PROD SSM mirror.
PROD (GenAiR-Cutter PROD mode): `--prod` regeneration with an `app_code`; SCM push → Jenkins on AWS (WIF `iac-sa`) → `main` → pro.
