Caption. PoC-equivalent low-code path from the GenAiR low-code docs (Conversational Agents = renamed Dialogflow CX: generative playbook,
data store tool, Google Chat integration), the GenAiR template exports, the ARB deck (slides 2, 4) and the ARD (FP1–FP6).
Employees ask in a Google Chat space; the Chat integration (or, per ARD FP1, an Apps Script router) reaches an agent whose playbook
grounds Gemini answers on a Vertex AI Search data store fed from a GCS bucket (Phase 1 manual upload; Phase 2 Drive sync not built).
Two PoC Cloud Run tools are called from the playbook: Link Formatter and Row-Level Access Security (dormant); logs go to BigQuery (FP6).
Red frames: no GenAiR production template, IaC or CI path for Conversational Agents (GenAiR-Cutter offers Cloud Run / Agent Engine only;
console build and zip restore), the Dialogflow ↔ Chat connection was rejected in POD (`auth.creds.useNormalUserEUC`, handover §C,
observed with Dialogflow ES), the Apps Script route needs a VPC-SC ingress rule per user identity. The PoC agent export was not found: `source-gap`.
Inheritance and environments: the agent starts from the `genair-conversational-agent` exports of `Airbus/GenAiR` (github.airbus.corp). With no Cutter template, the PROD dev / int / pro projects (orange, GenAiR PROD model) would each receive a manual console restore of an export versioned on the Airbus SCM (GitLab or GitHub: open); no webhook, no Jenkins job and no IaC exist for this path. Project ids: unknown.
